Changes in the 2.0 adaptation:
- Retain only personal-time (/ptime) and flight (/fly) commands.
- Remove fake, compression, and aggregate-help commands.
- Build a clean replacement without MCStats or other telemetry.
- Change dawn to sunrise (23000) and add dusk for sunset (12000).
- Correct command validation, sender/target handling, and flight ordering.
- Replace the obsolete IDE-only build with Maven and compatibility tests.
See README.md and docs/not-modernized-commands.md for details.

Changes in the 2.1.0 adaptation by Trenly:
- Restore /compress with runtime-supported base logs/stems, bone blocks
  (bones on older servers), ingot/raw-ore blocks, and diamond blocks.
- Preserve legacy wood/dye variants and original-style command help.
- Add metadata-safe, storage-only, all-or-nothing inventory conversion.
- Restore EnableCompress and operator-default compress.* permissions.
- Restore /tcpack aggregate help and its tcpack.list permission.
- Compress iron/gold nuggets into ingots before block conversion, preferring
  nugget-derived ingots and preserving atomic inventory updates.
- Add redstone dust and lapis lazuli block compression, including legacy lapis data.

